      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/71e660/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2020-07-14T16:39:47.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You can always read <a href=\"https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Podcasts\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">WT’s handy notes</a> as delightfully advertised in the episode. :3</p>\n<p>But if you want to actually listen, most of the episodes of the past year are individual issues and so mostly dependent on how much interest you have in the story being featured. So general interest episodes would be anything labelled “[character] Supporting Cast” or “[character] Villains”, the D-List Heroes episode, and also the Day in the Life Bunker episode as it’s sort of a Bunker Supplemental and the recent “Writers’ Room: Disparation Vol. 2 Issue <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#21</span>” because it’s kind of like a general thing about Sentinels Manga.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That is entirely true. Thanks for the tip! The main reason I asked is just because, like, being away for a year, there’s little way for me to tell what has and hasn’t been covered other than the notes or just listening to them all. I didn’t want to look like an idiot by asking, I dunno, “Hey so is Sky-Scraper and KNYFE a thing? I just have this vibe from them”, and then everyone says, “pfft, this loser doesn’t know about TLP175 and the hour-long smooching scene”.</p>",
