    {
      "id": 231271,
      "name": "Jeysie",
      "username": "Jeysie",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
      "created_at": "2020-07-14T17:15:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"The Girl With No Name\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n The Girl With No Name:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The main reason I asked is just because, like, being away for a year, there’s little way for me to tell what has and hasn’t been covered other than the notes or just listening to them all. I didn’t want to look like an idiot by asking, I dunno, “Hey so is Sky-Scraper and KNYFE a thing? I just have this vibe from them”, and then everyone says, “pfft, this loser doesn’t know about TLP175 and the hour-long smooching scene”.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>In that case, the questions section of Episode <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#144</span> - Writers’ Room: Justice Comics, Vol. 1, Issue <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#527</span> might interest you. No, seriously.</p>\n<p>The also serious answer is that the hodge-podge nature of the new mostly-story-based format means it’s hard to give a general recommendation of what episode to watch. Especially since the questions sections have turned into sort of mini-Editor’s Notes that are sometimes as much about follow up questions from previous episodes as they are about the feature characters of the present episode. :&gt;</p>\n<p>I’ve been thinking of how to restructure the Podcast wiki index to reflect it being harder lately to quickly pick out what an episode involves from the title alone, but it’s going to take some brainstorming.</p>",
